    "message": "docs: patches is an OSS command, not a Pro one\n\nThree places said otherwise: the gotcha claiming `ix patches` is an unknown\ncommand, the `[Pro]` marker on its routing-table row, and the \"only the first\nthree work without Pro\" line above that table.\n\nThe gotcha is replaced with the constraint that matters going forward — do not\nput `patches` back in `PRO_COMMANDS`, because a stub for a command that exists\nin OSS shadows the real implementation and does it silently.\n\nThe routing row now shows `--format llm`, which this command has supported all\nalong and which the format guidance immediately above the table tells agents to\nprefer when they are reading the output themselves.",
